       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual starting dose is 2.5\u20135 mg. A dose this high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. In overdose it can also cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nCould you check whether one of these was intended?\n- **5 mg once daily**, the standard starting dose\n- **10 mg once daily**, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg once daily**, a lower starting dose, often used for frail patients or those on other antihypertensives\n\nIf 50 mg is correct, for example because of a specific protocol, tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though it would likely need pharmacist or prescriber verification. If you give me the intended dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
